G1519.def:
**εἰς**,
_prep. with accusative, _
expressing entrance, direction, limit, **into, unto, to, upon, towards, for, among** (Lat. in, with accusative).
I. Of place.
1. After verbs of motion;
(a) **of entrance into**: [[Mat.8.23; 9.7|Mat.8:23, 9:7]], [[Mrk.1.45|Mrk.1:45]], [[Luk.2.15; 8.31|Luk.2:15, 8:31]], al.;
(b) of approach, **to** or **towards**: [[Mrk.11.1|Mrk.11:1]], [[Luk.6.8; 19.28|Luk.6:8, 19:28]], [[Jhn.11.31; 21.6|Jhn.11:31, 21:6]], al.;
(with) before pl. and collective nouns, **among**: [[Mrk.4.7; 8.19, 20|Mrk.4:7, 8:19, 20]], [[Luk.11.49|Luk.11:49]], [[Jhn.21.23|Jhn.21:23]], al.;
(d) Of a limit reached, **unto, on, upon**: [[Mat.8.18; 21.1|Mat.8:18, 21:1]], [[Mrk.11.1; 13.16|Mrk.11:1, 13:16]], [[Luk.14.10|Luk.14:10]], [[Jhn.6.3; 11.32|Jhn.6:3, 11:32]], al.; with accusative of person(s) (as in Ep. and Ion.), [[Act.23.15|Act.23:15]], [[Rom.5.12; 16.19|Rom.5:12, 16:19]], [[2Co.10.14|2Co.10:14]];
(e) **elliptical**: ἐπιστολαὶ εἰς Δαμασκόν, [[Act.9.2|Act.9:2]] ἡ διακονία μου ἡ εἰς Ἱ., [[Rom.15.31|Rom.15:31]] metaphorically, of entrance into a certain state or condition, or of approach or direction towards some end (Thayer, B, i, 1; ii, 1), εἰς τ. ὄνομα, M, _Pr._, 200.
2. Of direction;
(a) **after verbs of seeing**: [[Mat.6.26|Mat.6:26]], [[Mrk.6.41|Mrk.6:41]], [[Luk.9.16, 62|Luk.9:16, 62]], [[Jhn.13.22|Jhn.13:22]], al.; metaphorically, of the mind, [[Heb.11.26; 12.2|Heb.11:26, 12:2]], al.;
(b) **after verbs of speaking**: [[Mat.13.10; 14.9|Mat.13:10, 14:9]], [[1Th.2.9|1Th.2:9]], al.
3. After verbs of rest;
(a) **in "pregnant" construction, implying previous motion **(cl.; see WM, 516; Bl., §39, 3; M, _Pr._, 234f.): [[Mat.2.23; 4.13|Mat.2:23, 4:13]], [[2Th.2.4|2Th.2:4]], [[2Ti.1.11|2Ti.1:11]], [[Heb.11.9|Heb.11:9]], al.;
(b) by an assimilation general in late Gk (see Bl., M, _Pr._, ll. with) = ἐν: [[Luk.1.44; 4.23|Luk.1:44, 4:23]], [[Act.20.16; 21.17|Act.20:16, 21:17]], [[Jhn.1.18|Jhn.1:18]] (but see Westc, in l.), al.
II. Of time, **for, unto**;
1. accentuating the duration expressed by the accusative: εἰς τ. αἰῶνα, [[Mat.21.19|Mat.21:19]] εἰς γενεὰς καὶ γ., [[Luk.1.50|Luk.1:50]] εἰς τ. διηνεκές, [[Heb.7.3|Heb.7:3]], al.
2. Of a point or limit of time, **unto, up to, until**: [[Mat.6.34|Mat.6:34]], [[Act.4.3; 25.21|Act.4:3, 25:21]], [[Php.1.10; 2.16|Php.1:10, 2:16]], [[1Th.4.15|1Th.4:15]], [[2Ti.1.12|2Ti.1:12]]; of entrance into a future period, σεις τὸ μέλλον (see: μέλλω), **next (year)**, [[Luk.13.9|Luk.13:9]] (but with _ICC_, in l.); εἰς τ. μεταξὺ σάββατον, **on the next Sabbath**, [[Act.13.42|Act.13:42]] εἰς τὸ πάλιν (see: πάλιν, [[2Co.13.2|2Co.13:2]]
III. Of result, after verbs of changing, joining, dividing, etc.: στρέφειν εἰς, [[Rev.11.6|Rev.11:6]] μετας-, [[Act.2.20|Act.2:20]], [[Jas.4.9|Jas.4:9]]; μεταλλάσσειν, [[Rom.1.26|Rom.1:26]] σχίζειν εἰς δύο, [[Mat.27.51|Mat.27:51]], al.; predicatively with εἴναι, [[Act.8.23|Act.8:23]]
IV. Of relation, **to, towards, for, in regard to** (so in cl., but more frequently in late Gk., εἰς encroaching on the simple dative, which it has wholly displaced in MGr.; Jannaris, _Gr._, §1541; Robertson, _Gr._, 594; Deiss., _BS_, 117f.): [[Luk.7.30|Luk.7:30]], [[Rom.4.20; 15.2, 26|Rom.4:20, 15:2, 26]], [[1Co.16.1|1Co.16:1]], [[Eph.3.16|Eph.3:16]], al.; ἀγάπη εἰς, [[Rom.5.8|Rom.5:8]], al.; χρηστός, [[Eph.4.32|Eph.4:32]] φρονεῖν εἰς, [[Rom.12.16|Rom.12:16]] θαρρεῖν, [[2Co.10.1|2Co.10:1]]
V. **Of the end or object**: εὔθετος εἰς, [[Luk.14.34|Luk.14:34]] σόφος, [[Rom.16.19|Rom.16:19]] ἰσχύειν, [[Mat.5.13|Mat.5:13]] εἰς τοῦτο, [[Mrk.1.38|Mrk.1:38]], al.; ἀφορίζειν εἰς, [[Rom.1.1|Rom.1:1]] indicating purpose, εἰς φόβον, [[Rom.8.15|Rom.8:15]] εἰς ἔνδειξιν, [[Rom.3.25|Rom.3:25]] εἰς τό, with inf. (= ἵνα or ὥστε; Bl., §71, 5; M, _Pr._, 218ff.): [[Mat.20.19|Mat.20:19]], [[Rom.1.11|Rom.1:11]], [[1Co.9.18|1Co.9:18]], al.
VI. **Adverbial phrases**: εἰς τέλος, εἰς τὸ πάλιν, etc (see: τέλος, πάλιν, etc.).
(AS)

G1520.def:
**εἷς **
ιά, ἕν, genitive ἑνός, μιᾶς, ἑνός,
cardinal numeral, **one**;
1. **one**, as opposite to many: [[Mat.25.15|Mat.25:15]], [[Rom.5.12|Rom.5:12]], [[1Co.10.8|1Co.10:8]], al.; as subst., [[Rom.5.15|Rom.5:15]], [[Eph.2.14|Eph.2:14]]; id. with genitive partit., [[Mat.5.19|Mat.5:19]], al.; before ἐκ (ἐξ), [[Mrk.14.18|Mrk.14:18]], [[Jhn.6.8|Jhn.6:8]], al.; metaphorically, of union and concord, [[Jhn.10.30; 17.11|Jhn.10:30 17:11]], [[Rom.12.4-5|Rom.12:4-5]], [[Php.1.27|Php.1:27]]; ἀπὸ μιᾶς (B1., § 44, 1), [[Luk.14.18|Luk.14:18]] with neg., εἷς. . . οὐ (μή), more emphatic than οὐδείς, no one, none (cl.), [[Mat.5.18; 10.29|Mat.5:18 10:29]], [[Luk.11.46; 12.6|Luk.11:46 12:6]].
2. Emphatically, to the exclusion of others;
(a) **a single (one)**: [[Mat.21.24|Mat.21:24]], [[Mrk.8.14|Mrk.8:14]]; absol., [[1Co.9.24|1Co.9:24]], al.; οὐδὲ εἷς, [[Mat.27.14|Mat.27:14]], [[Jhn.1.3|Jhn.1:3]], [[Rom.3.10|Rom.3:10]], al.;
(b) **one, alone**: [[Mrk.2.7; 10.18|Mrk.2:7 10:18]], [[Luk.18.19|Luk.18:19]];
(with) **one and the same**: [[Rom.3.30|Rom.3:30]], [[1Co.3.8; 11.5; 12.11|1Co.3:8 11:5 12:11]], [[1Jn.5.8|1Jn.5:8]].
3. In late Gk., with weakened force, = τις or indef. art. (of. _Heb._ אֶחָד, [[Gen.22.13|Gen.22:13]], al.; see B1., § 45, 2; M, _Pr._, 96 f.): [[Mat.8.19; 19.6|Mat.8:19 19:6]], [[Rev.8.13|Rev.8:13]], al.; εἷς τις (Bl., l.with), [[Luk.22.50|Luk.22:50]], [[Jhn.11.49|Jhn.11:49]]
4. **Distributively**: εἷς καστος (cl.), [[Luk.4.40|Luk.4:40]], [[Act.2.6|Act.2:6]], al.; εἷς . . . καὶ εἷς (cl., εἷς μὲν . . . εἷς δέ), [[Mat.17.4|Mat.17:4]], [[Mrk.9.5|Mrk.9:5]], [[Jhn.20.12|Jhn.20:12]], al. (cf. LXX and use of _Heb._ אֶחָד, [[Exo.17.12|Exo.17:12]], al); ὁ εἷς . . . ὁ ἕτερος (ἄλλος) = cl. ὁ μὲν (ἕτερος) . . . ὁ δέ (ἕτερος), [[Mat.6.24|Mat.6:24]], [[Luk.7.41|Luk.7:41]], [[Rev.17.10|Rev.17:10]]; καθ᾽ εἷς, εἷς κ. είς (in which καθ᾽ is adverbial, or the expression formed from the analogy of ἕν καθ᾽ ἔν; M, _Pr._, 105), **one by one, severally**: [[Mrk.14.19|Mrk.14:19]], [[Rom.12.5|Rom.12:5]], al.; εἷς τὸν ἕνα = ἀλλήλους (B1., 45, 2; M, _Pr._, 246), [[1Th.5.11|1Th.5:11]]
5. As ordinal = πρῶτος (like _Heb._ אֶחָד; Bl., § 45, 1; M, _Pr._, 95 f.), **first**: [[Mat.28.1|Mat.28:1]], [[Mrk.16.2|Mrk.16:2]], al
(AS)

G1577.def:
**ἐκκλησία**, -ας, ἡ
(ἐκ-καλέω), [in LXX chiefly for קָהָל, otherwise for one of its cogn. forms ;]
1. prop., **an assembly** of citizens regularly convened (in Thuc., ii, 22, opposite to σύλλογος, _a concourse_): [[Act.19.32, 39, 41|Act.19:32, 39 41]].
2. In LXX of **the assembly, congregation, community** of Israel ([[Deu.4.10; 23.2|Deu.4:10 23:2]], al.): [[Act.7.38|Act.7:38]], [[Heb.2.12|Heb.2:12]]" (LXX) .
3. NT, esp. of an assembly or company of Christians, a **(the) church**;
(a) **of gatherings for worship**: [[1Co.11.18; 14.19, 34, 35|1Co.11:18 14:19, 34 35]];
(b) **of local communities**: [[Act.8.3|Act.8:3]], [[1Co.4.17|1Co.4:17]]; with name added, [[Act.8.1|Act.8:1]], [[Rom.16.1|Rom.16:1]], [[1Th.1.1|1Th.1:1]], al.; pl., [[Act.15.41|Act.15:41]], [[1Co.7.17|1Co.7:17]]; τ. Χριστοῦ, [[Rom.16.16|Rom.16:16]] τ. Ἀσίας, [[1Co.16.19|1Co.16:19]] τ. ἁγίων, [[1Co.14.33|1Co.14:33]] εἰπο]ν τ. ἐκκλησίᾳ, [[Mat.18.17|Mat.18:17]] (but see Hort, _Ecclesia_, 10); of a house-congregation (_DB_, i, 431a), [[Rom.16.5|Rom.16:5]], [[1Co.16.19|1Co.16:19]], [[Col.4.15|Col.4:15]], Phm 2;
(with) **of the whole body of Christians**: [[Mat.16.18|Mat.16:18]], [[1Co.12.28|1Co.12:28]], [[Eph.1.22|Eph.1:22]], [[Php.3.6|Php.3:6]], al.; τ. θεοῦ, [[Act.20.28|Act.20:28]] (Κυρίου, T, R, mg.), [[1Co.15.9|1Co.15:9]], [[Gal.1.13|Gal.1:13]], [[1Ti.3.15|1Ti.3:15]]; ἐ. προτοτόκων ἀπογεγραμμένων ἐν οὐρανοῖς, [[Heb.12.23|Heb.12:23]]
_SYN._: συναγωγή, which see (see Tr., _Syn._, §i; _DB_, i, 426; Hort, _Ecclesia_, esp. 4ff., 107ff.; Hamilton, _People of God_, ii, 37ff.; reff. s.vv. "Church," "Congregation," in _DB_ and _DCG_; Cremer, 332). (AS)

G1506.def:
**εἰλικρινής**, -ές,
[in LXX: Wi 72^ kB * ;]
**unalloyed, pure** (Lat. sincerus; see _DCG_, ii, 635a);
(a) **of unmixed substances**;
(b) **of abstract ideas**;
(with) **of ethical purity**: [[Php.1.10|Php.1:10]], [[2Pe.3.1|2Pe.3:1]].†
_SYN._: ἁγνός (which see), καθαρός, cf. Tr., _Syn._: §lxxxv; _DB_, iv, 176a; Cremer, 378; Westc. on [[1Jn.3.3|1Jn.3:3]] (AS)
